  "text": "```verilog\nmodule isochronous_spill_register #(\n    parameter WIDTH = 8\n)(\n    input              src_clk_i,\n    input              src_rst_ni,\n    input              src_valid_i,\n    output             src_ready_o,\n    input  [WIDTH-1:0] src_data_i,\n    input              dst_clk_i,\n    input              dst_rst_ni,\n    output             dst_valid_o,\n    input              dst_ready_i,\n    output [WIDTH-1:0] dst_data_o\n);\n\n    // Stage 0 (first register)\n    reg [WIDTH-1:0] stage0_data;\n    reg             stage0_valid;\n\n    // Stage 1 (second register)\n    reg [WIDTH-1:0] stage1_data;\n    reg             stage1_valid;\n\n    // Source domain: stage0\n    // src_ready_o is high when stage0 is empty, or when stage0 is full but stage1 is empty\n    // Actually, for a 2-deep buffer:\n    // - If stage0 is empty, we can accept.\n    // - If stage0 is full, we can accept only if stage1 is empty (so we can shift).\n    // But wait, in a standard 2-stage pipeline with valid/ready:\n    // Stage 0 accepts when it's empty OR when it can push to stage 1.\n    // Stage 0 can push to stage 1 when stage1 is empty OR when stage1 can push to dst.\n    \n    // Let's define the handshake properly.\n    // src_ready_o: source can send\n    // dst_valid_o: destination has data\n    // dst_data_o: destination data\n    \n    // The buffer has 2 slots.\n    // Slot 0: stage0\n    // Slot 1: stage1\n    \n    // src_ready_o = !stage0_valid || (stage0_valid && !stage1_valid)\n    // Actually, if stage0 is valid and stage1 is valid, we can't accept.\n    // If stage0 is valid and stage1 is empty, we can accept (and shift).\n    // If stage0 is empty, we can accept.\n    \n    // So: src_ready_o = !stage0_valid || !stage1_valid\n    \n    // dst_valid_o = stage1_valid\n    // dst_data_o = stage1_data\n    \n    // In dst_clk domain:\n    // If stage1_valid && dst_ready_i, then stage1 becomes empty.\n    // If stage0_valid && !stage1_valid, then stage1 gets stage0's data, stage0 becomes empty.\n    // If stage0_valid && stage1_valid && dst_ready_i, then stage1 becomes empty (consumed), \n    //   and stage0 moves to stage1? No, that's not right for a simple shift register.\n    \n    // Let me reconsider. A 2-deep FIFO with valid/ready:\n    // \n    // In dst_clk:\n    //   - If dst_ready_i && stage1_valid: stage1_valid <= 0\n    //   - If stage0_valid && !stage1_valid: stage1_data <= stage0_data, stage1_valid <= 1, stage0_valid <= 0\n    //   - If stage0_valid && stage1_valid && dst_ready_i: \n    //       stage1_valid <= 0 (consumed)\n    //       stage1_data <= stage0_data\n    //       stage0_valid <= 0\n    //   - If stage0_valid && stage1_valid && !dst_ready_i: nothing changes\n    //   - If !stage0_valid && stage1_valid && dst_ready_i: stage1_valid <= 0\n    //   - If !stage0_valid && !stage1_valid: nothing\n    //   - If !stage0_valid && stage1_valid && !dst_ready_i: nothing\n    //   - If stage0_valid && !stage1_valid && dst_ready_i: \n    //       stage1_data <= stage0_data, stage1_valid <= 1, stage0_valid <= 0\n    //       (same as above, dst_ready doesn't matter since stage1 was empty)\n    \n    // Wait, but stage0 is in src_clk domain and stage1 is in dst_clk domain.\n    // This is a CDC problem. The clocks are related (integer ratio), so we can use\n    // a simple synchronizer approach, but for valid/ready with related clocks,\n    // we need to be careful.\n    \n    // Actually, for related clocks (integer ratio), we can use a simple approach:\n    // - stage0 is clocked by src_clk\n    // - stage1 is clocked by dst_clk\n    // - We need to synchronize the valid signal from src to dst domain\n    \n    // But the problem says \"related clocks\" which means they have a fixed integer ratio.\n    // For a 2-deep spill buffer between related clocks, a common approach is:\n    // - Use a 2-stage pipeline where each stage is in its own clock domain\n    // - Synchronize the valid bit using a 2-flop synchronizer\n    \n    // However, for related clocks, we can also use a simpler approach if the ratio is known.\n    // But since the ratio isn't specified, let's use a standard CDC approach.\n    \n    // Let me reconsider the architecture:\n    // \n    // src_clk domain:\n    //   - stage0_data, stage0_valid\n    //   - src_ready_o = !stage0_valid || (stage0_valid && stage1_empty_synced)\n    //   - When src_valid_i && src_ready_o: stage0_data <= src_data_i, stage0_valid <= 1\n    //   - When stage0_valid && stage1_empty_synced: stage0_valid <= 0\n    //\n    // dst_clk domain:\n    //   - stage1_data, stage1_valid\n    //   - dst_valid_o = stage1_valid\n    //   - dst_data_o = stage1_data\n    //   - When stage1_valid && dst_ready_i: stage1_valid <= 0\n    //   - When stage0_valid_synced && !stage1_valid: stage1_data <= stage0_data_synced, stage1_valid <= 1\n    //\n    // Synchronization:\n    //   - stage0_valid needs to be synchronized to dst_clk\n    //   - stage0_data needs to be synchronized to dst_clk (or use a mux)\n    //   - stage1_empty needs to be synchronized to src_clk\n    \n    // For related clocks, a 2-flop synchronizer should work.\n    \n    // Let's implement this:\n    \n    // Synchronize stage0_valid to dst domain\n    reg stage0_valid_sync1;\n    reg stage0_valid_sync2;\n    \n    // Synchronize stage0_data to dst domain (use a register in dst domain)\n    reg [WIDTH-1:0] stage0_data_sync;\n    \n    // Synchronize stage1_empty to src domain\n    reg stage1_empty_sync1;\n    reg stage1_empty_sync2;\n    \n    // In dst_clk:\n    always @(posedge dst_clk_i or negedge dst_rst_ni) begin\n        if (!dst_rst_ni) begin\n            stage0_valid_sync1 <= 1'b0;\n            stage0_valid_sync2 <= 1'b0;\n            stage0_data_sync <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            stage1_data <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            stage1_valid <= 1'b0;\n        end else begin\n            stage0_valid_sync1 <= stage0_valid;\n            stage0_valid_sync2 <= stage0_valid_sync1;\n            \n            // Capture stage0_data when stage0_valid is high (synchronized)\n            if (stage0_valid_sync2) begin\n                stage0_data_sync <= stage0_data;\n            end\n            \n            // Stage1 logic\n            if (stage1_valid && dst_ready_i) begin\n                stage1_valid <= 1'b0;\n            end else if (stage0_valid_sync2 && !stage1_valid) begin\n                stage1_data <= stage0_data_sync;\n                stage1_valid <= 1'b0; // Will be set to 1\n                stage1_valid <= 1'b1;\n            end\n        end\n    end\n    \n    // In src_clk:\n    always @(posedge src_clk_i or negedge src_rst_ni) begin\n        if (!src_rst_ni) begin\n            stage0_data <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            stage0_valid <= 1'b0;\n            stage1_empty_sync1 <= 1'b1;\n            stage1_empty_sync2 <= 1'b1;\n        end else begin\n            // Synchronize stage1_empty to src domain\n            stage1_empty_sync1 <= !stage1_valid;\n            stage1_empty_sync2 <= stage1_empty_sync1;\n            \n            // Stage0 logic\n            if (src_valid_i && src_ready_o) begin\n                stage0_data <= src_data_i;\n                stage0_valid <= 1'b1;\n            end else if (stage0_valid && stage1_empty_sync2) begin\n                stage0_valid <= 1'b0;\n            end\n        end\n    end\n    \n    // Outputs\n    assign src_ready_o = !stage0_valid || stage1_empty_sync2;\n    assign dst_valid_o = stage1_valid;\n    assign dst_data_o = stage1_data;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
